  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A card is drawn from a standard deck of 52 cards. Find the probability that the card is:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "black or a heart",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
          "worked": "There are 26 black cards and 13 hearts, with no overlap.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{black or heart})&=\\frac{26}{52}+\\frac{13}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or heart})&=\\frac{39}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or heart})&=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "red or a club",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
          "worked": "There are 26 red cards and 13 clubs, with no overlap.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{red or club})&=\\frac{26}{52}+\\frac{13}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{red or club})&=\\frac{39}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{red or club})&=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "black or a king",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{13}$\n\nSubtract the two black kings counted in both events.",
          "worked": "There are 26 black cards, four kings and two black kings. Using the addition law:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{black or king})&=\\Pr(\\text{black})+\\Pr(\\text{king})-\\Pr(\\text{black and king})\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or king})&=\\frac{26}{52}+\\frac4{52}-\\frac2{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or king})&=\\frac{28}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or king})&=\\frac7{13}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "a king or a queen",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{2}{13}$",
          "worked": "There are four kings and four queens. These events are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{king or queen})&=\\frac4{52}+\\frac4{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{king or queen})&=\\frac8{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{king or queen})&=\\frac2{13}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "black or red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Every card is either black or red, and none is both.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{black or red})&=\\frac{26}{52}+\\frac{26}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{black or red})&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q20-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "red or a heart.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
          "worked": "Every heart is red, so the union is the event of drawing a red card.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{red or heart})&=\\frac{26}{52}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{red or heart})&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
